      "target": {
        "kind": "issue",
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "title": "trimMiddle: negative edge for maxLength<120 overflows output and reports impossible truncated count",
        "body": "`trimMiddle(text, maxLength)` in `src/clawsweeper-text.ts:11` computes `edge = Math.floor((maxLength - 120) / 2)`, which goes **negative** for any `maxLength < 120`. The head/tail slices then take from the wrong ends and the reported \"truncated N chars\" count exceeds the input length.\n\nRepro (property-test found via einsiedlerkrebs):\n```\ntrimMiddle(\"x\".repeat(25), 20)  =>  length 31 (> maxLength 20), text says \"truncated 125 chars\" for a 25-char input\n```\nInvariants violated: result length should be ~<= maxLength, and the reported removed-count should be in [0, text.length]. Guard `edge` to a sane minimum (and/or short-circuit when `maxLength` is below the header overhead).",
        "author": "anagnorisis2peripeteia",
